course: dictionary
lesson: 8837
title: Shipboard: life on a ship
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Look inside a word for smaller words you already know. Shipboard is made of ship and board. «On board» means on or aboard a vessel, so shipboard means on a ship.
explain: The word after shipboard tells you what it is describing. «Shipboard life» is life on a ship, and «a shipboard party» is a party held on a ship. When it describes a thing like this, shipboard is an adjective.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, the Sea Rat says, «Seawards first and then on shipboard, and so to the shores that are calling me!» The word seawards and the idea of faraway shores are the clues: he is travelling by sea, so on shipboard means on a ship.
explain: People today more often say on board or aboard. Shipboard sounds a little old-fashioned, so you will find it most in older stories and books about voyages.
fact: Shipboard means on or aboard a ship.
fact: Shipboard can be a noun, as in «on shipboard», or an adjective before a noun, as in shipboard life.
fact: Shipboard life can include sleeping in bunks or hammocks, eating in the galley, and practising fire and lifeboat drills.
fact: «Shipboard» is a little old-fashioned; people today more often say «on board» or «aboard».
fact: A good check is to swap in «on a ship» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Seawards first and then on shipboard, and so to the shores that are calling me!» What does on shipboard mean here? | Under the sea | On a train | In a shop | *On a ship
exercise: Ella says shipboard life means life in a shop. What is shipboard life really? | Life in a forest full of tall trees | Life in a fast car on a busy road | *Life on a ship, such as sleeping in bunks and eating in the galley | Life in a shop by the seaside
exercise: Which phrase means the same as on shipboard in everyday English? | on the moon | *on board | under the bed | in the garden
test: A shipboard party is a party held where? | In a cinema | *On a ship | In a school hall | On a mountain top
test: Which word is made from two smaller words you know, ship and board? | ancient | treacherous | curt | *shipboard
exam: In «shipboard life», is shipboard a noun or an adjective? | Adverb only | Verb | *Adjective, because it describes life | Noun only
